From: Snuffpig <181518943+Snuffpig@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915, ALSA: hda/hdmi: Fix HBR passthrough and multichannel LPCM over Gen12 DP-to-HDMI PCON

Fix HBR bitstream passthrough (TrueHD Atmos, DTS-HD MA) and multichannel
LPCM transitions on Intel Gen12 Tiger Lake systems routed through a DP-to-HDMI
PCON (Parade PS185):

- Preserve HSW_AUD_CFG bit 29 (AUD_CONFIG_N_VALUE_INDEX = 1 for DP mode) and
  restore timestamps before enabling AUDIO_OUTPUT_ENABLE, waiting >= 45 ms on
  drain and one VBlank on 0 -> 1 transitions and post-InfoFrame DIP arming.
- Gate AUDIO_OUTPUT_ENABLE teardown on actual per-pin transport transitions
  (non_pcm, hbr, rate, channels), invalidating cached state on hotplug/ELD
  notifications, bus resets, suspend, and teardown errors.
- Mute pin output amps on cleanup/close and across transport transitions
  until post-InfoFrame VBlank completes, while reconciling AC_DIG1_NONAUDIO,
  AC_DIG3_ICT, AC_PINCTL_EPT, full 32-byte InfoFrames, and DEV_SEL=0.

